    "result_text": "All 288 tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented AUDIT logging for successful owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), the single endpoint (`POST /api/owners`) that creates owners.\n\nThe change:\n- Added a dedicated logger named `AUDIT` (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`).\n- After `saveOwner` succeeds (so both the generated `id` and `membershipNumber` are populated), it logs the authenticated user (from `SecurityContextHolder`, falling back to `\"anonymous\"`), the new owner's id, and its membership number at INFO level.\n\nLogging happens after the save completes, so it only records genuinely successful creations \u2014 validation failures, quota rejections, and duplicate errors throw before reaching the log statement. The new `Cp19Tests` acceptance test and all 288 tests in the suite pass.",
